1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,840
One, do not ask about any grievance.

2
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,400
Two, do not ask about death.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,320
It's no use...let go...

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,280
Hang in there, Davis...

5
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:22,880
Geez!

6
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,800
What's wrong with you?

7
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,880
Don't look so scared.

8
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:30,880
Did you have a nightmare?

9
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:33,600
I just woke up and saw your face up close.

10
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,880
Of course I'm scared.

11
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,320
Was my face dirty?

12
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,440
I'll bring a girl home and scare you.

13
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,040
What is this?

14
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:46,800
I asked Uncle Kim to check
your luck with romance.

15
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:50,480
He said you'll have bad luck this year.

16
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:53,880
Your room is also in the "illness state".

17
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:57,160
Uncle Kim told me to display something
made of metal

18
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:00,120
and can make a sound to dispel
your misfortune.

19
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,320
Don't make me listen to the sutras.

20
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:06,320
What if you stop the bad luck,
but I end up in a monastery?

21
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:11,280
Listen, bad luck with romance is not a joke.

22
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,840
It can be quite serious, OK?

23
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:16,040
My bad luck with romance is over.

24
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,680
Romance to me is a fleeting cloud.

25
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:22,960
You'll be my only sweetheart, OK?

26
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,040
I'm only getting old.

27
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:28,400
You're divorced. Don't sound like
it's no big deal.

28
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,840
I thought once you got married,

29
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,080
someone can look after you.

30
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:34,360
Then I can enjoy a life of leisure.

31
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:37,600
But in less than a year,

32
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:40,400
you got a divorce and moved back home.

33
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:45,440
I thought you'd give me a grandchild,

34
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:50,160
But it was only my wishful thinking.

35
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:54,200
This is driving me mad.

36
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:59,920
I don't know what to do.

37
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,080
Chow time!

38
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,920
Congee with preserved egg and pork! Great!

39
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,480
It tastes different!

40
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,480
Why? You don't like it?

41
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:29,160
Not exactly. Nice to have a change.

42
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,520
Just tell me if you don't like it.

43
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,600
I won't make it again.

44
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,320
Don't say that.

45
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,800
I'll eat anything you make, Mom.

46
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,080
I need to go...

47
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,440
Wait...

48
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,000
More amulets for bad romance?

49
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,280
For evil spirits.

50
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,800
To ensure you're safe and things go well.

51
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:50,960
Keep it on you.

52
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,360
OK...

53
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,200
I had things to do tonight.
No dinner for me.

54
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:54,840
Bye!

55
00:03:57,040 --> 00:04:00,240
In doing the design, I took into
consideration the owner's preferences.

56
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,000
On this wall that is purposely left blank,

57
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,400
I added these shelves

58
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:05,120
for the owner's favorite perfumes,

59
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,880
so that not only is the space
visually relaxed,

60
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,160
the smell is also allowed to precipitate.

61
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,520
Cut! OK!

62
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:14,520
Davis, when you get to the sofa,

63
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,960
remember to mention the brand.

64
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:16,760
Sure.

65
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:19,720
The windowsill looks empty.

66
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,720
You have any props?

67
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,920
They're all here.

68
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,200
Lam, you have real flowers?

69
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,760
Lam-lam.

70
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:36,520
Angie!

71
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,120
Angie is also a writer.

72
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,640
I have urgent business to take care of.

73
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,640
Angie will take over.

74
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,320
What a coincidence!

75
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,720
You know each other?

76
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,320
Great! Have a nice chat.

77
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,160
I'll go wrap things up.

78
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:55,720
Sure!

79
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,560
I didn't expect you to fill in.

80
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,080
You got flowers? It's not Valentine's Day.

81
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:03,800
No, it's a prop.

82
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,800
I studied this flat.

83
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:08,080
The design is rather stripped back,

84
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,520
before the owner moves in,

85
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,440
it may seem rather empty and plain,

86
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,200
that's why I brought flowers.

87
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:19,960
Wifey!

88
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:21,840
Hubby?

89
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,760
You bought flowers?

90
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:27,680
Blessed are the pompon mums,

91
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,640
they give a new home a warm welcome.

92
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,600
You talk in rhymes now?

93
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:34,960
Why are you so happy?

94
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:39,160
I've been trying to fix the flowers
but I still don't like them.

95
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,960
I guess it's a problem with the flowers.

96
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,880
A flat must have real flowers.

97
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:46,320
But they're so hard to keep.

98
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:48,240
We'll just keep changing them

99
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:49,640
to ensure their freshness.

100
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,280
Great!

101
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,600
Be careful!
Thanks.

102
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,200
Thank you for your help.

103
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,440
Or the shoot wouldn't have gone so well.

104
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,400
To teamwork?

105
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,760
We have a crew car, where are you going?

106
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:12,080
I'll ask them to drop you.

107
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,880
No thanks. At this hour,

108
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,160
it's easier for me to leave on my own.

109
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,880
Right...at this hour,

110
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:22,120
you should be at your hang out, the bar.

111
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,360
It gives me inspiration.

112
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:27,320
Yup, pretty girls are inspirational.

113
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,280
It's good to relax.

114
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,160
Go ahead. I still have work to do.

115
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,440
You need to relax too.

116
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,120
Don't be so uptight about work.

117
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,600
I'm going. Bye!

118
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,200
Bye!

119
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,120
Hey, where were we?

120
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,120
Where's Pi? Just you?

121
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:00,920
Exactly!

122
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:03,080
He came out of the men's room
and went back inside.

123
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,440
Why? Weak kidneys?
Is he OK?

124
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,880
He's with a girl.

125
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:13,360
That girl over there also needs help
to the toilet.

126
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:16,600
Here's your chance.

127
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:21,840
Hi...what do you think of this place?

128
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:25,040
The designer should have good taste.

129
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,000
I find it a bit stuffy.

130
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:31,080
Why don't we go somewhere else?

131
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,120
I'm quite happy with the ventilation.

132
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:33,880
Feel free to leave.

133
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,880
Such a waste, pal!

134
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,880
Your wife used to hold you back.

135
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:44,160
Now? That's a crime to give up
a chance like that.

136
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:46,760
I came here to catch my breath, not to eat.

137
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,320
You must eat something you feel like eating.

138
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,040
Quality, OK?

139
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,520
Don't eat anything out of convenience.

140
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,440
Set some criteria.

141
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,800
Right...he likes home cooking.

142
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,160
He doesn't want MSG.

143
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,720
Something of a hipster?

144
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:04,640
Davis, thanks for the renovation.

145
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,280
This set of shooters is on the house.

146
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:07,960
I designed it based on the theme.

147
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,960
Grab one, don't just stand there.

148
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,040
Great...
Thank you...

149
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,680
Cheers!
Cheers!

150
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,200
Not bad...

151
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:20,560
Nice!

152
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:24,320
What? Not again!

153
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,920
No way, it's impossible...

154
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,880
What's going on?

155
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:30,360
That's Sylvia Siu Zi-yiu. She's a hit.

156
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:31,440
Another one...

157
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:35,000
I saw her on TV. She's the promising witch.

158
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:37,400
She's always livestreaming or go on TV.

159
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,560
More importantly, she's pretty.

160
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:43,000
After the renovation, I hired her
as a resident guest.

161
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:45,400
It's a gimmick to draw in the crowd.

162
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,960
Take your pick. I don't believe
you can guess it right every time.

163
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:06,600
It's responding...
Is it possible?

164
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:08,040
Let's see...

165
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:17,200
She's right again...awesome!

166
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:19,240
We're almost out of booze.

167
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:22,800
If you want to play another game,
pop another bottle.

168
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,840
No way. You must have fixed it.

169
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:27,120
How could you guess the highest card
every time?

170
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:30,680
Sir, if you can't hold your alcohol,

171
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:33,240
don't force yourself to drink.

172
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,680
Not that I don't want to drink,

173
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:35,960
I want you to drink with me.

174
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,360
You can't hold your alcohol,

175
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,200
you also can't hold your temper.

176
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,080
What do you mean, you bloody witch?

177
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,240
Would you believe you can't
leave here alive?

178
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,160
What are you doing? Interfering?

179
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,720
Chill, pal!

180
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:49,680
This chic knows black magic.

181
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,600
Last time I pissed her off...

182
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:56,160
You should go.

183
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,360
For you.

184
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,000
Thanks.

185
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:09,200
As a psychic, you know black magic?

186
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:11,280
Why do you ask?

187
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:14,760
I told that guy you know black magic.

188
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,520
I pissed you off before,

189
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,400
now I lose all my bets,

190
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,840
I have sleep paralysis every night,

191
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,120
I can't walk straight

192
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,840
and was plagued with hidden diseases.

193
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,520
Like what?

194
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,200
That's the second question.

195
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:28,800
You need to satisfy my request first.

196
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:45,000
For your first request,

197
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,000
I assume you like to drink.

198
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:50,800
But your second request of taking me home,

199
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:53,080
don't tell me you're a stalker.

200
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:58,520
I am...afraid that guy would come back
to give you trouble.

201
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,360
That's why I'm following you
and protecting you.

202
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,160
You live here?

203
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:12,960
This is where I live and give people advice.

204
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:17,040
Are you interested in coming up
and be my bodyguard?

205
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:22,920
I am, but a shifu told me I have
bad luck with romance.

206
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,640
You're such a pretty girl,

207
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,240
I'm afraid such close contact
may land me in trouble.

208
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,880
Thanks.

209
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:32,680
Pretty girls may have nothing to do
with your romance.

210
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:35,440
You may have the luck of dispelling
a disaster.

211
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,360
Give me a hair.

212
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:39,840
To perform black magic?

213
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,600
To get your undying devotion.

214
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:07,760
Shifu was right...

215
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,480
I'm in trouble?

216
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:15,200
You will repeatedly run into a girl

217
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:17,640
who has great affinity with you.

218
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:23,560
It's likely...she's the one who will
go through thick and thin with you.

219
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:27,480
How do I know who is the right girl for me?

220
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:38,880
Golden sun, snow in May and burning sky

221
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:42,080
are signs you'll see when
the right girl shows up.

222
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,120
Golden sun...

223
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:49,320
Are you OK?

224
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,040
I'm tired.

225
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,200
Maybe you should go.

226
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:54,880
Are you sure you're OK?

227
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,760
Subscribe to my channel.

228
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:01,160
I'm fine if you see new updates.

229
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,600
OK, don't stay up late.

230
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:08,160
Get some rest. I'm going. Bye!

231
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:09,480
Bye!

232
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:28,800
I'm so happy to do this livestreaming
for all of you today.

233
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,120
Don't complain Yan Piggy doesn't
take care of her fans.

234
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:33,920
I came here with my bestie for a massage
and I'm still livestreaming.

235
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:36,480
This is what Yan Piggy usually wears.

236
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:37,680
It's very simple, right?

237
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:41,000
Excuse me, not so hard.

238
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:46,480
Wow! Thank you, Yan simp for
sending the golden rocket.

239
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:48,560
It's so cool and Yan Piggy loves it.

240
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,520
But most, most, most importantly,

241
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:54,920
remember to comment, like and share. Bye!

242
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:57,560
Thank you.

243
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:03,840
Hey, Missie, you work in the morning,

244
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,480
and livestream at night,

245
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:08,080
even while you're enjoying a massage.

246
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,160
Are you really that busy?

247
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,240
You don't understand the fans.

248
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:13,640
They want to see their idol play video games

249
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:16,280
as well as how she lives a normal life.

250
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:18,280
You had the filter on,

251
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:20,000
how can they see the normal you?

252
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:24,160
Not everyone is a natural beauty
like you, Miss Man Nga-kei.

253
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:27,280
You're coming with me to buy a uniform.

254
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:29,920
Again? You have so many already.

255
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,200
There are all types of nurses.

256
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,520
Even cats are either black or white.

257
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,920
Yan Piggy's best outfit is always
the next one.

258
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,360
Since Yan Piggy has everything all set up,

259
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,920
Kei Piggy can't say no, right?

260
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:45,000
How dare you say no?!

261
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:48,040
Your life used to revolve around
your husband,

262
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,360
and it was impossible to see you.

263
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:51,120
Now that you're single again,

264
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,760
it's time you dote on me.

265
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:57,720
Did you know I prefer to stay home
to binge on TV dramas and read?

266
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,520
I can play video games with you,

267
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,880
but I don't want to go out.

268
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:05,280
But you would go to Hell and back
for you know who.

269
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:08,600
OK...I'll go. I'll go with you.

270
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:10,080
I'll go with you later...
Great!

271
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,160
Wear it with me.

272
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,320
I'll help you shop...

273
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,200
What are you looking for?

274
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,880
Tangerine peel.

275
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,360
It's over there.

276
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,600
Hello, son?

277
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:29,680
Mom, did you send me the wrong address?

278
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:30,760
I can't find it.

279
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:34,000
Of course not! Look again.

280
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:37,440
Do you have to buy your tangerine peel
from that shop?

281
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:39,600
If you don't want the trouble,

282
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:42,240
next time I make congee,
you better not complain.

283
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,440
Go look...

284
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:44,680
When did I complain...?

285
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:51,440
Auntie!

286
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,240
Oh, Angie!

287
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:55,760
No need to look again.

288
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,240
You bought it for me?

289
00:15:58,320 --> 00:16:01,160
No, I was shopping with a friend.

290
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,040
It was on the way.

291
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,280
You're so sweet.

292
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,920
That brat is useless.

293
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:09,200
I gave him the address and he can't find it.

294
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:12,720
He goes grocery shopping with you
all the time.

295
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:13,800
He's a good son.

296
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,680
How is he?

297
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:18,320
He's such a fussy eater.

298
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:20,560
I used a different tangerine peel
in the congee

299
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,880
and he frowned.

300
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:26,280
That's why I came here to buy
the one you used.

301
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,400
How are you lately?

302
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,560
The same. Not too bad.

303
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:36,040
A bit busy because I have a show on air.

304
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,080
Auntie, when you cook,

305
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:40,480
you can add tangerine peel on anything.

306
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:42,400
I used to make tea for Davis

307
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,440
and he liked it a lot.

308
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,920
When it comes to cooking,

309
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,760
my hat's off to you.

310
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:53,040
Hello? No need, I found it...

311
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,160
From the herb store next to the market.

312
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,840
OK...see you at the corner.

313
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:07,240
(There was a man)

314
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:12,640
(That sailed the seas)

315
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:18,240
(He left his woman)

316
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,640
(behind to leave)

317
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:29,160
(He left his children)

318
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,320
(to mourn alone)

319
00:17:37,520 --> 00:17:39,280
(But don't you cry)

320
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:45,200
(He's coming home)

321
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:50,640
(But don't you cry)

322
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:56,600
(He's coming home)

323
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:03,480
Mom, this is the kind...

324
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:06,080
Last time you said a change of taste.

325
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,760
Now you want more of the same?

326
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:10,160
Anything you cook will taste good.

327
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,680
What a sweet talker.

328
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:17,080
Pissed? OK, I'll do the dishes.

329
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:20,720
Better not. I don't want to lose more bowls.

330
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:24,000
You better go pack your things.

331
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,640
I only broke a few bowls,

332
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,160
you're throwing me out already?

333
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:31,400
The suitcase has been sitting there
since you moved back home.

334
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,920
If I didn't touch it for a few months,

335
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,720
that means the things are useless.

336
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:36,880
Just toss them.

337
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:39,200
No, they are your things.

338
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,680
Sort them out yourself.

339
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,440
OK...I'll do it.

340
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,120
The design...

341
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,560
(One and a half years ago)

342
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:15,280
Well? Are you finished?

343
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:18,400
Wifey, your smile is so stiff.

344
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:19,960
Try to look more natural.

345
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:21,480
Who's your wife?

346
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,480
You, sooner or later.

347
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:24,720
What's wrong with calling you that?

348
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:27,760
Hurry up, there are people around.

349
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:31,120
I'm painting. We have nothing to hide.

350
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,320
Don't look so embarrassed.

351
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:38,840
Hey, it's raining.

352
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:44,160
Cover it up!

353
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,720
I told you the Observatory predicted
rain for today.

354
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:51,840
But the maple leaves look their best today.

355
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:53,880
Luckily, it didn't get wet.

356
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,680
But you're all wet, silly goose!

357
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,840
You're so stuck up,

358
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:34,360
hanging your paintings on the whole wall.

359
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:37,480
They're all paintings of you.

360
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:39,680
You begged me to marry you
because you like my paintings.

361
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:42,040
What? I begged you?
Of course you did.

362
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:44,240
You turned things around.

363
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:46,480
If you didn't beg, why would I propose?

364
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:47,800
Stop...

365
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:02,000
The cotton tree wadding slipped
through my hands,

366
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:06,520
the same hands you held and dropped.

367
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,360
(Sent)

368
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:42,680
Sylvia!

369
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:45,920
What's up?

370
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:53,440
Where are we going?

371
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:55,520
Sh...don't ask.

372
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:04,760
(Chan Sin To Memorial Primary School)

373
00:23:15,880 --> 00:23:17,280
You know how to use a feng shui compass?

374
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:18,920
You know eastern and western
fortune telling.

375
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:23,080
All things have a spiritual essence
and are inter-related.

376
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:24,480
The world is big

377
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:26,840
and there's so much we don't know.

378
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:29,000
I always study things that seem interesting.

379
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,720
What's that?

380
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,520
This magnetic field detector

381
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:36,760
can detect the changes in the
magnetic field around us.

382
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:40,480
It changes color when it detects
something abnormal.

383
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,800
Red means it's nearby.

384
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:46,040
We're looking for spirits?

385
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,800
We're doing a field test.

386
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:33,960
Both your compass and the machine
had a strong reaction.

387
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,640
Does that mean there was something...?

388
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:40,360
A classroom in Chan Sin To
Memorial Primary School

389
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:43,680
had an electrical leakage because
the switch was in disrepair.

390
00:24:43,760 --> 00:24:46,360
During lunch break, several kids
were hurt from the electric shock.

391
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:50,160
One of the girls stepped on a plastic ball,

392
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:53,480
and died from hitting her head
against the wall.

393
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:54,920
A plastic ball?

394
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:58,320
The baby doll we just saw was a girl.

395
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:02,280
It's late now, stepping on the ball
is not unusual.

396
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:06,000
Dolls are either a boy or a girl.

397
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:09,560
Who's there? You're not supposed to be here.

398
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:10,720
Run...

399
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:21,560
Being chased by humans
is scarier than by a ghost.

400
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,160
Sometimes, humans are scarier than ghosts.

401
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:39,920
You're pretty even when you're making faces.

402
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:41,840
It's fitting for tonight's theme.

403
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:43,680
For our first attempt to seek out a spirit,

404
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:45,360
we should commemorate it with a post.

405
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:46,960
Why don't you tag me?

406
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:50,640
Sylvia Siu Yiu 1111.

407
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:54,280
OK...done!

408
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:20,120
Nice picture. Give it a like.

409
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:20,840
Hey!

410
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:24,320
What? Who's that?

411
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:27,800
My ex-wife.

412
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:30,960
Sorry! Should I unlike it?

413
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:32,040
No need.

414
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:35,120
You had a big fight?

415
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:39,280
No, we split on good terms.

416
00:26:39,320 --> 00:26:41,160
That was three months ago.

417
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:44,600
But lately, I kept running into her.

418
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:48,560
Take this picture for instance.

419
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:51,280
I saw the cotton tree wadding,

420
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:52,760
got out of the car to take a picture.

421
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:54,320
I didn't know she was there

422
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:56,280
and I showed up in her picture.

423
00:26:57,240 --> 00:27:00,120
I remember I didn't see her that day.

424
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:02,400
There was another time,

425
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:04,800
I was on a TV show to talk about a design.

426
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:09,000
She was filling in for my colleague
as a copywriter.

427
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:11,840
Maybe it's your fate.

428
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,400
It's May now.

429
00:27:15,120 --> 00:27:18,280
Is the cotton tree wadding
considered "snow in May"?

430
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:22,600
Last time she brought sunflowers
when she filled in for my colleague.

431
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:23,840
Could that be "golden sun"?

432
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:26,120
What about "burning sky"?

433
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:28,080
Will there be a fire next time we meet?

434
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:29,760
If you don't believe it,

435
00:27:29,840 --> 00:27:32,080
maybe you overlooked something.

436
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:34,280
What have I overlooked?

437
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:40,560
"The cotton tree wadding slipped
through my hands,"

438
00:27:40,600 --> 00:27:43,240
"the same hands you held and dropped."

439
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:46,280
She knew you were in the picture.

440
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:49,320
By saying that, she's obviously
not yet over you.

441
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:52,440
She's known to be sensitive.

442
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:56,640
Maybe she wrote that because
of what's in that picture.

443
00:27:57,520 --> 00:27:59,920
When I saw her recently,

444
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,000
I didn't sense anything.

445
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,440
What about you? Are you over her?

446
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,920
Honestly, she's a good wife.

447
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:14,000
It was my fault, I'm not cut out
to be a married man.

448
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:17,720
Marriage is about finding
the right other half.

449
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:20,520
If things are not over for you,

450
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:22,360
you are somewhere still connected.

451
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,280
Connected?

452
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:28,880
We haven't sold the flat we're still
making payments on.

453
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:30,280
She's still living there.

454
00:28:30,320 --> 00:28:31,360
Is that considered a connection?

455
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:34,880
Tangible or not, that's still a connection.

456
00:28:37,360 --> 00:28:42,600
Romance and bad luck are often inseparable.

457
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:47,480
Passionate love, like fireworks,

458
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:50,120
is dazzling and exciting

459
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:52,320
but also dangerous.

460
00:28:54,320 --> 00:28:57,960
Ordinary love, like temperature,

461
00:28:58,040 --> 00:29:00,080
is still water that runs deep.

462
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:05,360
You want fireworks or temperature?

463
00:29:08,040 --> 00:29:10,960
Destiny is often not your choice.

464
00:29:16,120 --> 00:29:17,200
I'll drop you off...

465
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:28,320
Try to scoop it out in one piece.

466
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:29,520
We need to steam that later.

467
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:32,440
Brother On, is this really good?

468
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:35,200
When I scoop this out, I usually toss it.

469
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:36,440
You'll soon find out.

470
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:38,640
Look, Brother On!

471
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:41,480
What? Hey...

472
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:43,040
Stop the camera...

473
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:45,120
Sorry...I didn't mean it!

474
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,280
Bowie, did you scald yourself?

475
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:47,240
I'm fine.

476
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:49,200
Be careful...Brother On, I'm sorry,

477
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:50,600
we may need to do the dish again.

478
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:52,720
But we need to hand over
the studio in an hour.

479
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:54,600
The beef stew takes at least two hours.

480
00:29:54,680 --> 00:29:56,880
We have two other dishes to make
according to the rundown.

481
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:58,320
What can we do?

482
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:01,520
It's OK. Brother On,
leave the beef stew to me.

483
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:03,280
Ka-kei, get someone to clean this up.

484
00:30:03,360 --> 00:30:03,960
Sure!

485
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:06,280
Director, you can film Brother On and Bowie

486
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,360
making the next dish.

487
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,760
Sang and I will take care of
everything else.

488
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:09,640
Sang, come here...

489
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:10,240
OK!

490
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:15,840
Here's the honey...

491
00:30:15,920 --> 00:30:16,440
Thanks, Sang.

492
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:43,560
Brother On, I love this beef stew.

493
00:30:43,600 --> 00:30:47,040
It's tender and the acidity of the wine

494
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:48,360
has a hint of sweetness,

495
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:49,840
giving it complexity.

496
00:30:49,920 --> 00:30:51,440
I'll make other dishes for you next time.

497
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:52,360
Promise?

498
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:55,360
See you on the next Gourmet Chef Encore.

499
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:56,440
Bye!

500
00:30:56,880 --> 00:30:58,240
Cut! Good take!

501
00:30:58,840 --> 00:31:00,320
OK...thank you.

502
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:02,960
You're a good cook for someone so young!

503
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:04,080
Thanks, Brother On!

504
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:07,280
She truly rose to the occasion.

505
00:31:07,360 --> 00:31:09,200
Without you, I wouldn't know
what to do, Angie.

506
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:11,640
Yes, thank goodness you were here.

507
00:31:11,720 --> 00:31:14,240
Stop teasing me. I'm the writer,

508
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:16,400
It's my job to solve problems.

509
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:17,600
I get paid to do this.

510
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:20,520
But why did you add honey?

511
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:22,960
It wasn't on the ingredients list.

512
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:25,280
Honey contains proteinase

513
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:27,440
that can make the beef tender
in a short time.

514
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:29,000
Pineapple juice can do that too.

515
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:32,040
OK...let's clear out.

516
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:34,040
Thank you...
Let's pack up...

517
00:31:34,120 --> 00:31:35,120
Thank you...

518
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:38,720
Angie!

519
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:44,160
Sesame paste and sweet potato soup?

520
00:31:44,240 --> 00:31:47,320
Nobody knows me better than you,
Yip Lai-yan.

521
00:31:47,400 --> 00:31:48,080
You bet!

522
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:55,400
Angie, let's go see the flame trees
and have a picnic.

523
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:57,640
That looks gorgeous!

524
00:31:57,720 --> 00:32:00,080
But I'm really busy lately.
I may not make it, sorry!

525
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:14,480
I know, only Davis is king.

526
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:15,320
Says who?

527
00:32:15,760 --> 00:32:18,760
You couldn't stop smiling
when he liked your picture.

528
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:20,560
You're still in love with Davis.

529
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:22,880
Even the picture you post
had him in the background.

530
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:25,880
I admit I'm still in love with him.

531
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:29,000
Just learn to let go...

532
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:32,760
(Delete)

533
00:32:32,800 --> 00:32:33,920
What are you doing?

534
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:35,480
Chopping down the tree.

535
00:32:35,680 --> 00:32:39,280
See? Look at the other beautiful
trees waiting for you.

536
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:42,240
I'll invite other good catches for you.

537
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:43,200
You must show up.

538
00:32:47,920 --> 00:32:52,080
On today's live cast, I'll show you
how to make a romance orgonite pyramid.

539
00:32:52,120 --> 00:32:55,920
The key to making the pyramid
is how to distribute the crystals.

540
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:02,240
Next, you add UV gel

541
00:33:02,320 --> 00:33:05,960
and put it under the lamp
for about five to six minutes.

542
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:09,000
You can also add natural ingredients,

543
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:14,160
such as the petals from the
blooming flame trees.

544
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:18,120
Then this person will be thinking of you
at all times.

545
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:24,840
I heard the flame trees in
Lam Shing Country Park are gorgeous.

546
00:33:32,520 --> 00:33:33,160
Off I go!

547
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:54,960
Angie, where are you going?

548
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:58,280
Lam Shing Country Park.

549
00:33:58,360 --> 00:34:01,360
I saw on the news the flame trees
are in full bloom.

550
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:03,280
What a coincidence! I'm heading out there.

551
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:04,840
Hop in. I'll give you a lift.

552
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:06,760
OK.

553
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:10,720
Seat belt.

554
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:24,120
Is everything OK with you lately?

555
00:34:24,800 --> 00:34:25,400
OK!

556
00:34:31,560 --> 00:34:32,560
Shall we go look?

557
00:34:33,440 --> 00:34:34,160
Sure!

558
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:36,720
Angie!

559
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:41,920
What a coincidence, Davis!

560
00:34:42,400 --> 00:34:44,640
We found the perfect spot...

561
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:47,320
We brought food. Want to join us?

562
00:34:48,080 --> 00:34:49,600
No thanks. I'll walk around by myself.

563
00:34:50,720 --> 00:34:51,400
OK!

564
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:52,720
Let's go!
Bye!

565
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:53,360
Bye!

566
00:35:30,240 --> 00:35:31,800
Angie, want something to drink?

567
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:33,920
Thanks.

568
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:38,480
Liz said you're a writer for the TV station

569
00:35:38,520 --> 00:35:39,840
and you also do research.

570
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:40,800
What programs are you working on?

571
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:44,040
Just finished a cooking show

572
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:45,560
and looking for new ideas right now.

573
00:35:45,600 --> 00:35:47,040
How about a dating reality show?

574
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:48,240
It's a big hit nowadays.

575
00:35:48,280 --> 00:35:51,000
Something like Romance Hit &amp; Run,

576
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:52,760
or Living Under the Same Roof.

577
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:54,440
The name tells you what kind of
program it is

578
00:35:54,480 --> 00:35:55,720
and will catch eyeballs for sure.

579
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:56,720
What do you think?

580
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:57,880
Good idea!

581
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:01,240
Excuse me, I need to use the toilet.

582
00:36:01,320 --> 00:36:02,240
OK.

583
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:05,800
Now she's on the run.

584
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,640
(There was a man)

585
00:36:15,680 --> 00:36:17,800
(That sailed the seas)

586
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:23,120
(He left his woman)

587
00:36:26,040 --> 00:36:28,160
(behind to leave)

588
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:35,920
Golden sun, snow in May and burning sky

589
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,440
are signs you'll see when
the right girl shows up.

590
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:43,120
This is the prettiest of all the trees.

591
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:46,440
Yeah. The canopy is so big

592
00:36:46,520 --> 00:36:50,160
it looks like the sky is on fire.

593
00:36:52,200 --> 00:36:55,200
Too bad, I don't have a model today.

594
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:04,600
What kind of pose do you want?

595
00:37:16,800 --> 00:37:19,600
You're actually my perfect model.

596
00:37:20,480 --> 00:37:22,600
If we were not married,

597
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:23,960
I'm sure we'll make a good team.

598
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,080
It's raining!

599
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:34,160
It's just a light drizzle.

600
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:35,760
The painting will get wet.

601
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:45,400
Leave it, Angie!

602
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:47,680
Angie...

603
00:37:58,920 --> 00:37:59,920
Angie...

604
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:03,240
Angie...

605
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:04,840
Davis...

606
00:38:08,040 --> 00:38:10,480
Davis...

607
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:25,400
Angie...
Davis...

608
00:38:26,280 --> 00:38:29,760
It's no use, let go...

609
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:31,320
Hang in there...

610
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:33,680
Remember when we first got married,

611
00:38:33,760 --> 00:38:35,600
Mother drew a lot for us?

612
00:38:36,640 --> 00:38:41,200
It says if we don't give up,

613
00:38:41,240 --> 00:38:43,760
we'll always land on our feet.

614
00:38:45,040 --> 00:38:47,840
Hang in there, Davis...

615
00:39:38,760 --> 00:39:45,360
Davis...

616
00:39:47,160 --> 00:39:48,360
Help!

617
00:39:49,600 --> 00:39:52,800
Davis...wake up...

618
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:55,080
Help, anyone?

619
00:39:56,280 --> 00:40:00,400
Davis...wake up...

620
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:03,120
Anyone out there...
